==================================================
1. DOMAIN ENTITIES
==================================================

Create the following entities in:

src/NovaBanking.Application/

- Customer
- CustomerCredential
- CustomerSession
- Account
- Transaction
- Loan
- CreditCard

Follow the exact fields and data types specified in the case study.

Required schema:

Customer:
- CustomerId int PK
- CustomerNumber nvarchar(20)
- FullName nvarchar(120)
- Email nvarchar(150)
- Phone nvarchar(20)
- Status nvarchar(20)
- CreatedOn datetime2 UTC

CustomerCredential:
- CredentialId int PK
- CustomerId FK
- PinHash nvarchar(500)
- FailedAttemptCount int
- LockedUntil datetime2 nullable
- LastSuccessfulLogin datetime2 nullable

CustomerSession:
- SessionId uniqueidentifier PK
- CustomerId FK
- TokenHash nvarchar(500)
- ExpiresOn datetime2
- RevokedOn datetime2 nullable
- CreatedOn datetime2

Account:
- AccountId int PK
- CustomerId FK
- AccountNumber nvarchar(30)
- AccountType nvarchar(30)
- LedgerBalance decimal(18,2)
- AvailableBalance decimal(18,2)
- Currency char(3)
- Status nvarchar(20)

Transaction:
- TransactionId bigint PK
- AccountId FK
- TransactionType nvarchar(20)
- Amount decimal(18,2)
- Description nvarchar(200)
- TransactionDate datetime2
- ReferenceNumber nvarchar(40)

Loan:
- LoanId int PK
- CustomerId FK
- LoanNumber nvarchar(30)
- LoanType nvarchar(40)
- SanctionedAmount decimal(18,2)
- OutstandingAmount decimal(18,2)
- InterestRate decimal(5,2)
- NextDueDate date
- Status nvarchar(25)

CreditCard:
- CreditCardId int PK
- CustomerId FK
- MaskedCardNumber nvarchar(20)
- CardType nvarchar(30)
- CreditLimit decimal(18,2)
- AvailableLimit decimal(18,2)
- OutstandingBalance decimal(18,2)
- MinimumAmountDue decimal(18,2)
- PaymentDueDate date
- Status nvarchar(20)

==================================================
2. RELATIONSHIPS
==================================================

Implement these relationships:

Customer
    1 -> 0..1 CustomerCredential
    1 -> many CustomerSessions
    1 -> many Accounts
    1 -> many Loans
    1 -> many CreditCards

Account
    1 -> many Transactions

Every foreign key must be explicitly configured.

Use appropriate navigation properties.

Configure sensible delete behavior.

Do not use cascade delete in a way that could accidentally destroy large portions of customer financial data.

